1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,740
What happens when a company receives a supplier invoice that doesn't match what was ordered?

2
00:00:06,740 --> 00:00:15,726
In accounts payable, invoices, purchase orders, and receiving logs constantly arrive with discrepancies: price overcharges, quantity shortages, or tax variances.

3
00:00:15,726 --> 00:00:19,320
Traditional ERP systems easily flag the math mismatch.

4
00:00:19,320 --> 00:00:23,364
But detecting an exception is only half the battle.

5
00:00:23,364 --> 00:00:30,553
The hardest part is deciding what to do next: Has this supplier billed this way before?

6
00:00:30,553 --> 00:00:33,698
Did an authorized manager negotiate a waiver?

7
00:00:33,698 --> 00:00:39,090
And is that previous approval still valid under current company procurement policy?

8
00:00:39,090 --> 00:00:41,824
That's why we built LedgerMind.

9
00:00:41,824 --> 00:00:50,574
An invoice exception isn't just a math error—it's an operational decision requiring context, precedent, and accountability.

10
00:00:50,574 --> 00:01:00,963
LedgerMind combines deterministic three-way matching with persistent institutional memory powered by Hindsight, version-governed policy evaluation, and fast Groq inference.

11
00:01:00,963 --> 00:01:05,338
Our central innovation: LedgerMind never blindly follows history.

12
00:01:05,338 --> 00:01:10,806
It cross-examines remembered precedents against the company's governing procurement rules.

13
00:01:10,806 --> 00:01:18,462
When past habit conflicts with policy, policy constraints govern, and the reviewer is alerted.

14
00:01:18,462 --> 00:01:22,290
This policy-versus-precedent intelligence is LedgerMind's core breakthrough.

15
00:01:22,290 --> 00:01:29,745
Here in the live application, the Overview tracks six discrepancy categories across twenty benchmark scenarios.

16
00:01:29,745 --> 00:01:36,703
Both our local Hindsight vector engine and SQLite operational database are online and healthy.

17
00:01:36,703 --> 00:01:42,170
Through New Invoice Intake, teams can create or import new invoices.

18
00:01:42,170 --> 00:01:47,636
Here we submit an invoice for Nova Tech Supplies: invoice INV-NOVA-2025-002.

19
00:01:47,636 --> 00:01:55,588
The purchase order specified one thousand rupees, but the vendor billed eleven hundred across ten units.

20
00:01:55,588 --> 00:02:08,510
With eighteen percent GST, LedgerMind instantly calculates a discrepancy of eleven hundred and eighty rupees, and syncs it immediately to SQLite and the active Invoice Queue.

21
00:02:08,510 --> 00:02:12,617
In the Resolution Workbench, LedgerMind evaluates the discrepancy.

22
00:02:12,617 --> 00:02:22,886
With memory enabled, the agent checks governing policy POL-AP-002 and identifies that price variances exceeding contract rates require line-item adjustment.

23
00:02:22,886 --> 00:02:29,047
LedgerMind generates an EDITED proposal, resetting unit rates to the contract price.

24
00:02:29,047 --> 00:02:32,641
Crucially, the human reviewer retains full authority.

25
00:02:32,641 --> 00:02:37,262
We submit our review as an authorized AP Specialist.

26
00:02:37,262 --> 00:02:45,990
The decision, adjusted amount, and audit rationale are permanently saved to both SQLite and persistent Hindsight memory.

27
00:02:45,990 --> 00:02:50,182
Look closely at our Hindsight vector memory integration.

28
00:02:50,182 --> 00:02:55,945
For invoice INV-PI-2025-101 from Prabhav Infosystems, Hindsight performs live semantic recall.

29
00:02:55,945 --> 00:03:03,281
Notice the storage badge: every card displays 'Hindsight Vector DB' with verified live provenance.

30
00:03:03,281 --> 00:03:13,760
Our multi-pass evidence deduplication consolidates sub-facts from a single Zenith review into one card, preserving slots for direct Prabhav precedents.

31
00:03:13,760 --> 00:03:23,715
Cross-vendor precedents are clearly flagged with orange badges, while the invoice's own historical review is excluded from confidence scoring.

32
00:03:23,715 --> 00:03:36,290
In our Memory Comparison view, Memory OFF yields zero context, while Memory ON boosts confidence to seventy-five percent, grounded in three consistent prior decisions.

33
00:03:36,290 --> 00:03:41,692
Most enterprise tools stop at finding where the numbers don't add up.

34
00:03:41,692 --> 00:03:54,747
LedgerMind's value is in helping a human reviewer understand what the organization learned before, whether that precedent is still valid, and why a specific resolution is justified right now.

35
00:03:54,747 --> 00:04:02,400
It unites historical recall, policy conflict detection, explainable evidence, and human accountability into a coherent decision workflow.

36
00:04:02,400 --> 00:04:16,587
Building LedgerMind taught us a key architectural lesson: never interleave blocking health probes into asynchronous vector queries, and keep supplier tag taxonomies strictly isolated from corporate legal stopwords.

37
00:04:16,587 --> 00:04:22,160
Today, LedgerMind is a working prototype with manual and CSV intake.

38
00:04:22,160 --> 00:04:29,253
In the future, we envision native ERP connectors, automated OCR, and enterprise role-based access.

39
00:04:29,253 --> 00:04:36,347
LedgerMind helps finance teams move from detecting invoice exceptions to making consistent, policy-backed decisions.

40
00:04:36,347 --> 00:04:37,360
Thank you.
